<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Toluca Valley</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Toluca Valley is a high basin in the State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valley-of-mexico">Valley of Mexico</a>, drained by the upper Lerma river and centred on the city of Toluca. Before the Spanish conquest it was home to Matlatzinca, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otomi">Otomi</a> and Mazahua peoples. It was conquered in the 1470s by the Aztec <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Triple Alliance</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axayacatl">Axayacatl</a>, and lands there were assigned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlacopan">Tlacopan</a> and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tepanecs">Tepanec</a> allies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/toluca-valley.jpg" alt="Toluca Valley" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thelmadatter · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:VallyTolucaTeotenango.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
